well a warning from nevada's attorney  general scammers apparently demanding  payment by gift cards our bianca holmen  breaks down what you need to know so you  can protect yourself  we all dread the robo and fraudulent  calls at all hours of the day and night  but there are scammers pretending to be  legitimate businesses and government  agencies asking for payment by gift card  nevada attorney general aaron ford says  gift cards are not for making payments  for taxes fines bills or other types of  reimbursement criminals use gift cards  for payment because they're easy for  people to purchase at the store however  once a scammer has the card information  they can quickly use the funds and the  money cannot be recovered or traced here  are some tips so you don't become a  victim  first be weary of calls or emails from  anyone creating an urgent situation and  requesting a gift card  second the scammer may tell you to buy a  certain gift card and load money on it  remember the government will not ask you  to pay taxes or fines via gift card if  you paid a scammer with a gift card  report it to the company that issued the  card and file a complaint with a federal  trade commission bianca holman live  local now
 

